# TAMALE 3D
## MASTER UPGRADE: REALISM, GRAPHICS, CITY INFRASTRUCTURE, TRAFFIC, LAW ENFORCEMENT, NIGHTLIFE, MUSIC & IMMERSIVE GAMEPLAY

Act as a senior game development team consisting of:

- Senior game engine developer
- Three.js specialist
- React and TypeScript engineer
- 3D character artist
- Animation specialist
- Vehicle simulation engineer
- AI and NPC behaviour engineer
- Urban environment designer
- Traffic simulation engineer
- Game UI/UX designer
- Audio engineer
- Performance optimization engineer
- Quality assurance engineer

You are working on the EXISTING TAMALE 3D project.

TAMALE 3D is an open-world city life simulator based on Tamale, Northern Ghana.

The project currently uses React, TypeScript, Three.js, and Vite, and already contains a world engine, playable characters, NPC schedules, vehicles, traffic, roads, landmarks, businesses, interiors, jobs, economy, weather, music, and other gameplay systems.

## YOUR MISSION

Transform the existing TAMALE 3D project into a visually impressive, realistic, immersive, functional, and interconnected open-world city simulator.

The game should capture the experience of living, moving, working, socializing, transporting goods, driving, exploring, and enjoying city life in Tamale.

I want the game world to feel alive.

Characters should look like real humans.

Cars should look like real cars.

Motorcycles should look like real motorcycles.

Trucks should transport goods.

Roads should be properly connected.

Buildings must be aligned properly with the urban environment.

Traffic lights must work.

Police must enforce laws.

Players should be able to experience nightlife, enter clubs, listen to Northern Ghanaian music, dance, socialize, transport goods, complete jobs, encounter accidents, and navigate the city.

The city must have meaningful day and night life.

This is an upgrade to the existing project, not a new game.

